{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5552) from an automated code generation pipeline. The task is to implement `cmd/chgrp` for the go-unix-utils project, specifically implementing srd090 requirements R1.1 through R1.4 (core group-change and argument parsing). The deliverable is two new files: `cmd/chgrp/main.go` (the chgrp utility) and `cmd/chgrp/chgrp_test.go` (differential tests against the GNU `gchgrp` reference binary). The task explicitly excludes recursive traversal (R2.x) and verbose/output control (R3.x) which would be separate tasks.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `chgrp` utility verified via differential testing against Homebrew `gchgrp`\n   - SRD090 defines three requirement groups: R1 (group ownership change), R2 (recursive/symlink), R3 (output/exit codes)\n   - This task covers only R1.1-R1.4: argument parsing, GROUP resolution (name or numeric GID), applying group change, error handling, SIGPIPE, --help/--version\n   - `os.Chown(path, -1, gid)` to change group without modifying owner (-1 means keep current)\n   - `os/user.LookupGroup` for name-to-GID resolution, `strconv.Atoi` for numeric GIDs\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` must be called at start of main()\n   - `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary`, `RunDiffTests`, `DiffTest` struct for differential testing\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gchgrp\")` with `t.Skip` if not found\n   - Manual argument parsing (no cobra framework for cmd/ utilities)\n   - `--reference=RFILE` flag to copy group from a reference file\n   - Non-goal: `--preserve-root` must NOT be implemented\n   - Execution constitution enforces: E8 (40-line function limit), E9 (500-line file limit), E3 (no scope creep), E6 (non-goals enforcement)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd090-chgrp.yaml` (READ)\n     - Defines all chgrp requirements. Task scope is R1.1-R1.4 only.\n     - R1.1: Accept GROUP (name or numeric GID) + FILE... arguments, change each file's group\n     - R1.2: --reference=RFILE sets group to match RFILE's group\n     - R1.3: Process multiple FILE arguments\n     - R1.4: Exit 1 on errors, print to stderr, continue processing remaining files\n     - Non-goals: --preserve-root\n     - Package contract imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n   - `cmd/chmod/main.go` (READ - reference implementation)\n     - Shows the project's pattern for permission-change utilities\n     - Key patterns to follow:\n       - Copyright header format\n       - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` as first line of main()\n       - `options` struct for CLI flags\n       - Manual arg parsing with `parseArgs`, `handleSpecialArg`, `parseLongFlag`, `parseShortFlags`\n       - `--help` prints helpText and exits 0, `--version` prints versionText and exits 0\n       - `--` ends flag parsing\n       - `--reference=RFILE` handling with `strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--reference=\")`\n       - `processFile` → `processRecursive` or `applyAndReport` pattern\n       - `reportError` with silent suppression\n       - `formatErr` using `errors.AsType[*os.PathError]` for clean error messages\n       - Exit code tracking: start at 0, set to 1 on any error, exit at end\n\n   - `cmd/chgrp/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - chgrp utility with argument parsing, group resolution, ownership change\n   \n   - `cmd/chgrp/chgrp_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests against gchgrp reference binary\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was still in the reading/planning phase when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand exact requirements for R1.1-R1.4\n   - Read the chmod reference implementation to understand project patterns for similar utiliti